There is a difference between Nethack and the RPG games.  The RPG
games are designed to be played once. You are supposed to finish the
whole game once and then there is generally no incentive for you to
play it again because it goes the same way as before. In this case it
is very boring to restart a game from the beginning, so it is very
important to save the games and after dying resume it. This allows you
to win the game without getting bored.

This is not the case with nethack. Nethack is meant to be played again
and again. The game does not unfold the same way ever again. There is
no boredom in restarting games. Actually the initial game ie till you
finish the mines is probably the most interesting part of the game. I
normally find it a lot less interesting after completing the mines.
So save scumming is not really necessary.

The other question is winning. Obviously someone who completed the
game by save-scumming should not claim that they have won. Because
with save-scumming you will eventually finish the game. There is
nothing enjoyable about it. The real joy should come from winning the
game without save-scumming. Old timers (and even quite a few new ones)
realize this and consider it as bad form. But there is nothing
preventing you to do it.

I have done a lot of cheating in my early days. Initially, I had
modified the Nethack launcher script to automatically save the save
files, with new names, making scumming so much more easier. I
completed the game with it but it was really very boring. Then I
changed the code to always give me the Wand of Wishing with 99
charges, this also got boring very quickly. After this I changed the
initial character properties from a total of 75 to 100. This made a
wizard quite buff from the very beginning. It was not bad. Actually I
liked it a lot. But I wasn't learning anything.

After that came google groups and I found out RGRN, and there I
learned the pacifist protection racket.  I tried it a few times and
then quickly got better at nethack. Since then I have been playing
without any cheating. I did ascend quite soon after this (a wizard).
Although I never posted the YAFAP. After that I did not ascend
anything, because I get really bored in the gehennom. I must have
abandoned atleast a dozen characters in the gehennom. Arch, Tourist,
Healers, Monk. I also play very slowly, and I get a lot less time,
which means that a character in gehennom is left behind for a
